apes but  art works like these are essential for  him communicating his ideas to the wider  scientific  okay so he's classified the clouds from  these drawings but why do we care it's a  good question  so when Howard was working meteorology  was still a really young science and it  was still very much about gathering as  much data as you possibly could in as  many observations as you could and kind  of hoping that patterns would would  appear from those observations but  Howard's scheme allowed us to to start  to view the clouds in a scientific way  [Music]

